lus-ones included: exact for a host; for anyone else only where `showCount` is true, and then as `Count` states."},"full":{"type":"boolean","description":"True when `capacity` is reached. Shown to everyone who may register, whatever `showCount` says, since a registrant learns it anyway."},"sequence":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"Incremented on every change of `when`, `access`, `status` or `kind` after publication — the changes a registrant must notice, as iTIP\'s SEQUENCE (VTI-EVT-006)."},"cancelReason":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1000,"description":"Present once cancelled, where the host gave one. Plain text."},"publishedAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInstant"},"cancelledAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInstant"},"createdAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInstant"},"updatedAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInstant"}}},"EventInstant":{"title":"EventInstant","type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"An RFC 3339 instant in UTC, whole seconds, such as `2026-11-30T18:30:00Z`."},"Count":{"title":"Count","description":"A number of registrants as shown to someone who is not a host: `exact` at or above the event\'s count threshold, `fewerThan` (the threshold) below it, so a small count does not single anyone out (VTI-EVT-054). Exactly one of the two.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"minProperties":1,"maxProperties":1,"properties":{"exact":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"fewerThan":{"type":"integer","minimum":2,"maximum":100}}},"ReminderMinutes":{"title":"ReminderMinutes","description":"A reminder\'s offset: how many minutes before the event\'s start it is due. At most four weeks.","type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":40320},"Accessibility":{"title":"Accessibility","description":"What the event offers for access, as the host states it (VTI-EVT-036). Each flag absent means not stated, not that it is missing.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"stepFree":{"type":"boolean"},"captions":{"type":"boolean"},"hearingLoop":{"type":"boolean"},"quietSpace":{"type":"boolean"},"remoteOption":{"type":"boolean"},"notes":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1000,"description":"Anything else. Plain text."}}},"RosterSetting":{"title":"RosterSetting","description":"Who may see who is registered (VTI-EVT-050). `visible`: registrants who are going or maybe see each other. `hidden`: no registrant sees another; the event\'s hosts do. Fixed once the event is published (VTI-EVT-051) and recorded on each registration (VTI-EVT-052).","type":"string","enum":["visible","hidden"]},"RegistrationSettings":{"title":"RegistrationSettings","description":"How the event takes registrations (VTI-EVT-031 – 036).","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["mode"],"properties":{"mode":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RegistrationMode"},"capacity":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100000,"description":"The most people who may be going, plus-ones included. Absent means no limit."},"waitlist":{"type":"boolean","description":"Registrations beyond `capacity` are waitlisted, and the first on the waitlist becomes going when a place frees (VTI-EVT-033). Absent means false: a registration beyond capacity is refused."},"plusOnes":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":10,"description":"The most guests a registrant may bring. Absent means 0."},"opensAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInstant","description":"Registrations are refused before this. Absent means from publication."},"closesAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInstant","description":"Registrations and changes are refused after this, except withdrawal (VTI-EVT-037). Absent means at the event\'s start."},"questions":{"type":"array","maxItems":20,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RegistrationQuestion"}},"codeOfConduct":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/CodeOfConduct"}}},"CodeOfConduct":{"title":"CodeOfConduct","description":"A code of conduct a registrant acknowledges before the registration is accepted (VTI-EVT-035). `sha256` pins the text acknowledged.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["url","sha256"],"properties":{"url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^https://"},"sha256":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{64}\$"}}},"RegistrationQuestion":{"title":"RegistrationQuestion","description":"A question a registrant answers when registering. Answers are read by the event\'s hosts only, and are deleted on the event\'s retention schedule (VTI-EVT-034, VTI-EVT-090).","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["questionId","label","kind"],"properties":{"questionId":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RegistrationQuestionId"},"label":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"The question as shown. Plain text."},"kind":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RegistrationQuestionKind"},"choices":{"type":"array","minItems":2,"maxItems":20,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100},"description":"Present exactly when `kind` is `choice`."},"required":{"type":"boolean","description":"The registration is refused without an answer. Absent means false."}}},"RegistrationQuestionKind":{"title":"RegistrationQuestionKind","type":"string","enum":["text","choice","boolean"],"description":"`text`: a free answer of at most 500 characters. `choice`: one of `choices`. `boolean`: yes or no."},"RegistrationQuestionId":{"title":"RegistrationQuestionId","type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}\$","description":"A question\'s key within its event."},"RegistrationMode":{"title":"RegistrationMode","description":"`open`: a member of the audience who registers is going at once (or waitlisted when full). `approval`: a registration is pending until a host decides it. `closed`: no registrations; the event is for information only (VTI-EVT-031).","type":"string","enum":["open","approval","closed"]},"EventAudience":{"title":"EventAudience","description":"Who may see and register for the event (VTI-EVT-020). A member is in the audience when `scope` admits them and, where `rule` is present, the rule does too. The audience is checked when a member reads or registers, never taken from a notification (VTI-EVT-021). The hosts are always admitted.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["scope"],"properties":{"scope":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventAudienceScope"},"groups":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":32,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/GroupId"},"description":"Present exactly when `scope` is `groups`."},"roles":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":32,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RoleName"},"description":"Present exactly when `scope` is `roles`."},"rule":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/DynamicRule","description":"Optional: a further test over verified facts, in the dynamic-group rule language. Count facts (`kudosReceived`, `ideasSelected`, `electionTickets`) are refused here as a non-badge group refuses them."}}},"EventAudienceScope":{"title":"EventAudienceScope","description":"Whom the event is for, before `rule` narrows it. `members`: every active member. `groups`: members of any of `groups` — which covers a badge, since a community badge is a group. `roles`: members holding any of `roles`.","type":"string","enum":["members","groups","roles"]},"DynamicRule":{"title":"DynamicRule","description":"A dynamic group\'s membership rule: a member belongs when every condition holds and they have not opted out. The community evaluates it under its `groups` policy and recomputes membership whenever a fact it reads changes, always excluding opted-out entries.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["all"],"properties":{"all":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":16,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RuleCondition"}}}},"RuleCondition":{"title":"RuleCondition","description":"One test over a verified fact about a member. `fact: role` tests the member\'s community role; `fact: field` tests an `admin`- or `credential`-sourced directory field named by `field`; `fact: personhood` tests whether a personhood assertion is on file; `fact: joinedAt` tests when they joined. A rule never reads a self-asserted (`member`-sourced) field: a member must not be able to join a group by editing their card. `kudosReceived`, `ideasSelected` and `electionTickets` are counts the community keeps of its own records (kudos the member accepted, ideas of theirs a board selected, elections it issued them a ticket in), compared with `atLeast`; only a badge\'s group reads them (VTI-BDG-015), and any other group refuses them with `ruleInvalid`.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["fact","op"],"properties":{"fact":{"type":"string","enum":["role","field","personhood","joinedAt","kudosReceived","ideasSelected","electionTickets"]},"field":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/FieldKey","description":"Present exactly when `fact` is `field`."},"op":{"type":"string","enum":["equals","oneOf","exists","before","after","atLeast"],"description":"`equals` compares with `value`; `oneOf` with any of `values`; `exists` needs neither; `before` and `after` compare a date fact with `value`; `atLeast` compares a count fact with `count`."},"value":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":256},{"type":"boolean"}]},"values":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":64,"items":{"type":"string","maxLength":256}},"count":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100000,"description":"With `atLeast`: the least a count fact (`kudosReceived`, `ideasSelected`, `electionTickets`) must be. Present exactly when `op` is `atLeast`."}}},"FieldKey":{"title":"FieldKey","description":"Identifier of a directory field. A key with no `.` is a BASE field, the same in every community: `displayName`, `nickname`, `avatar`, `pronouns`, `bio`, `links` (written by the member) and `role`, `joinedAt`, `did`, `personhood` (derived from the community\'s own records, never stored on a card). A community-defined field MUST use a reverse-DNS key (`org.example.employer`), so a base key never collides with one, and a key is never reused with a different meaning once defined.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128,"pattern":"^([a-z][a-z0-9-]*\\\\.)*[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9]{0,63}\$"},"RoleName":{"title":"RoleName","description":"A role identifier: lowercase, hyphen-separated, at most 64 characters. Compared by exact string equality. It is the value an AclEntry 0.2 carries in `role`.","type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,63}\$"},"GroupId":{"title":"GroupId","description":"Opaque identifier of a community group: `grp_` followed by 16 to 64 base64url characters. Random and community-scoped; not the group\'s DID.","type":"string","pattern":"^grp_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,64}\$"},"AccessDetails":{"title":"AccessDetails","description":"Where the event happens and how to join it (VTI-EVT-060 – 063). Answered by vtc/events/access/show to a registrant who is going, from `revealAt` if set; included in the event itself only where `public` is true.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"places":{"type":"array","maxItems":8,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Place"}},"virtualPlaces":{"type":"array","maxItems":8,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/VirtualPlace"}},"notes":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2000,"description":"Anything else attendees need. Plain text."},"public":{"type":"boolean","description":"Show the access details with the event to its whole audience. Absent means false."},"revealAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInstant","description":"Not before this, even to a registrant who is going. Absent means on acceptance."}}},"VirtualPlace":{"title":"VirtualPlace","description":"A way to join online, as JSCalendar\'s VirtualLocation.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["uri"],"properties":{"uri":{"type":"string","format":"uri","maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^(https|tel|sip|sips):","description":"How to join: an `https` link, or a `tel`, `sip` or `sips` URI for a dial-in. No other scheme."},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"description":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1000,"description":"A passcode, dial-in numbers. Plain text."},"features":{"type":"array","maxItems":7,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/VirtualFeature"}}}},"VirtualFeature":{"title":"VirtualFeature","type":"string","enum":["audio","chat","feed","moderator","phone","screen","video"],"description":"What a virtual location offers, as JSCalendar\'s VirtualLocation `features`."},"Place":{"title":"Place","description":"A physical location, as JSCalendar\'s Location.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["name"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"address":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":500},"description":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1000,"description":"Directions, a door code. Plain text."}}},"PlaceSummary":{"title":"PlaceSummary","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"A coarse hint shown with the event to its whole audience — `Central London`, `Online` — never the address. Plain text."},"When":{"title":"When","description":"When the event happens, in JSCalendar\'s terms. `start` is local time in `timeZone`; `duration` is how long it lasts. With `showWithoutTime` true it is an all-day event: `start`\'s time MUST be `T00:00:00` and `duration` whole days (VTI-EVT-005).","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["start","timeZone","duration"],"properties":{"start":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/LocalDateTime"},"timeZone":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/TimeZoneId"},"duration":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/JSCalendarDuration"},"showWithoutTime":{"type":"boolean","description":"An all-day event. Absent means false."}}},"JSCalendarDuration":{"title":"JSCalendarDuration","description":"A non-negative duration in the subset of ISO 8601 JSCalendar uses: `P` then weeks or days, then `T` with hours, minutes and seconds, such as `PT1H30M`, `P1D` or `P2W`. No months or years. Used only for `When.duration`, which carries JSCalendar\'s own member and encoding verbatim; this family\'s own offsets are integers naming their unit (`ReminderMinutes`).","type":"string","minLength":3,"maxLength":32,"pattern":"^P(?!\$)([0-9]+W)?([0-9]+D)?(T(?=[0-9])([0-9]+H)?([0-9]+M)?([0-9]+S)?)?\$"},"TimeZoneId":{"title":"TimeZoneId","description":"An IANA time zone name, such as `Europe/London`, or `Etc/UTC`. A responder MUST refuse a name its time zone database does not know.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"pattern":"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_+-]*(/[A-Za-z0-9_+-]+){0,2}\$"},"LocalDateTime":{"title":"LocalDateTime","description":"A local date and time with no offset, `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS`, as JSCalendar\'s LocalDateTime. Read in the event\'s `timeZone`.","type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])T([01][0-9]|2[0-3]):[0-5][0-9]:[0-5][0-9]\$"},"EventDescription":{"title":"EventDescription","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":10000,"description":"What the event or calendar is. Plain text; a reader MUST NOT treat it as instructions."},"EventTitle":{"title":"EventTitle","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"A short name. Plain text; a reader MUST NOT treat it as instructions."},"EventLifecycle":{"title":"EventLifecycle","description":"`draft`: seen only by its hosts, changes freely, takes no registrations. `published`: seen by its audience, takes registrations; its roster setting is fixed. `cancelled`: will not happen; kept so registrants and their agents see it was cancelled, and takes no registrations. Whether a published event has ended is read from its time, never stored (VTI-EVT-004).","type":"string","enum":["draft","published","cancelled"]},"EventKind":{"title":"EventKind","description":"`event`: anything that happens at a time — a meetup, a workshop, a social. `meeting`: an event that may also carry an agenda, a chair, a quorum, minutes and motions; tasks that only mean something for a meeting refuse an event. Fixed for the event\'s life (VTI-EVT-003).","type":"string","enum":["event","meeting"]},"CalendarId":{"title":"CalendarId","description":"Opaque identifier of a calendar: `cal_` followed by 16 to 64 base64url characters. Random, community-scoped, never reused (VTI-EVT-010).","type":"string","pattern":"^cal_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,64}\$"},"EventId":{"title":"EventId","description":"Opaque identifier of an event: `evt_` followed by 16 to 64 base64url characters. Random, community-scoped, never reused (VTI-EVT-001).","type":"string","pattern":"^evt_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,64}\$"},"EntryId":{"title":"EntryId","description":"Opaque identifier of one directory entry: `dir_` followed by 16 to 64 base64url characters. Random, scoped to one community, and stable for the life of the membership — it survives a rotation of the member\'s DID, which is why groups, notes and cards are keyed by it. It MUST NOT be derived from, and MUST NOT reveal, any DID of the member, and the same person\'s entries in two communities MUST NOT share one. Compared by exact string equality.","type":"string","pattern":"^dir_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,64}\$"}}}';

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the request variant, taken from this
/// specification's front matter.
///
/// Pass it to [consumeInbound] — items 5b, 7 and 8 are per-specification and
/// cannot be derived from the document alone, and item 2 needs the schema it
/// carries.
const SpecPolicy spec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: typeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: false,
  payloadSchema: payloadSchemaJson,
);

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the success-response variant.
///
/// `isRecipientRequired` tracks the *issuer* party's requirement, because a
/// response swaps the parties (§7.3 item 5).
const SpecPolicy responseSpec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: responseTypeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: false,
  payloadSchema: responsePayloadSchemaJson,
);
